Image writer diagnostics for the missing ArtField relocation entry (q20-android research)

Two problems with the upstream diagnostic in FixupPointerArray:

1. Its LOG(FATAL) message is built with PrettyField, which reaches
   ArtField::GetTypeDescriptor -> GetDexFile ->
   GetDeclaringClass()->GetDexCache()->GetDexFile(). When the declaring class
   has no dex cache, which is exactly the state being reported, that
   dereferences NULL and the diagnostic is replaced by a SIGSEGV inside the
   logging code.
2. It does not say whether the declaring class is still a live, registered
   class or reclaimed memory, which is the question that decides where the bug
   is (GC roots versus the pruning pass).

Log the raw pointers and the class header words first, then the pretty names
only when they are safe to compute.

Also fixes the root cause found with that diagnostic on hardware: the prune
loop read fields through DexCache::GetResolvedField(), which returns nullptr
for fields of erroneous declaring classes. A boot class that fails
verification (quickened dex, e.g. android.icu.impl.PluralRulesLoader) keeps
its field in the resolved fields array, the class is pruned and reclaimed,
and FixupPointerArray later dies on the dangling ArtField. Read the raw
array element instead.

--- a/art/compiler/image_writer.cc
+++ b/art/compiler/image_writer.cc
@@ -657,6 +657,11 @@
